  <h2>Peer-reviewed publications</h2>

  <h3>Investor Behavior at the 52-Week High</h3>
  <p class="muted">
    Della Vedova, J., Grant, A. R., and Westerholm, P. J. (2023).
    <em>Journal of Financial and Quantitative Analysis</em>, 58(7), 2852-2889. (ABS 4, ABDC A*, FT50)
  </p>
  <p>
    Individual investors systematically misread the 52-week high as a reference price, generating asymmetric
    buying and selling pressure that predicts short-horizon return reversals.
  </p>

  <h3>Who Drives Momentum Returns? The Role Reversal of Trend-Seeking Households and Contrarian Institutions</h3>
  <p class="muted">
    Della Vedova, J., Grant, A. R., and Westerholm, P. J. (2025).
    <em>European Financial Management</em>. (ABS 3, ABDC A)
  </p>
  <p>
    Retail households drive conventional momentum returns through trend-following behavior, while institutions
    contrarian-trade against the momentum factor. Investor-class decomposition of the canonical cross-sectional
    momentum strategy.
  </p>

