  <h2>Work in progress</h2>

  <h3>Probability Weighting from Prediction Markets (with A. Grant)</h3>
  <p>
    Prediction markets provide a model-free measurement of probability weighting. A weekly panel of 233M trades
    yields a Prelec alpha of 0.651 for non-bot wallets, matching the Tversky-Kahneman (1992) experimental
    estimate almost exactly. Tests whether the prediction-market-implied weighting index predicts
    cross-sectional equity anomalies.
  </p>

  <h3>Political Uncertainty and the Cross-Section of Asset Returns: Evidence from Forward-Looking Prediction Markets</h3>
  <p>
    Prediction-market odds as a forward-looking proxy for political uncertainty and its incremental pricing
    relative to backward-looking uncertainty measures.
  </p>

